        "id": "U8-D3",
        "statement": "Validation scans the list once in list order and stops at the first order that fails any of the three checks (Value \u003C= 0, DayOfMonth \u003C 1 or \u003E 31, OrderId already seen). The repeated-id check names the later order (the one whose id an earlier order already used). Id equality is exact ordinal string equality, so \u0027rent\u0027 and \u0027RENT\u0027 are distinct orders. The date is checked only afterwards, through Ledger.setDate, which supplies DateInPast and accepts the current business date.",
        "basis": "evidence",
